# Remote Work and Flexible Arrangements Policy

**Document Type:** Corporate Policy
**Authority Level:** 1 (Authoritative)
**Policy Number:** POL-006
**Effective Date:** March 1, 2024
**Last Reviewed:** January 2026
**Owner:** Chief Human Resources Officer
**Classification:** Internal

---

## Purpose

This policy establishes guidelines for remote work and flexible working arrangements at Nexus Industries, supporting employee productivity and work-life balance while maintaining operational effectiveness.

---

## Scope

This policy applies to all Nexus Industries employees whose roles can be performed remotely. Certain positions may be designated as on-site only based on job requirements.

---

## Work Arrangement Types

| Type | Description | Frequency |
|------|-------------|-----------|
| **On-Site** | Work primarily at Nexus facility | 5 days/week |
| **Hybrid** | Combination of remote and on-site | 2-3 days on-site |
| **Remote** | Work primarily from home/approved location | Occasional on-site |
| **Flexible Hours** | Non-standard work hours | Per arrangement |

---

## Eligibility

### Eligible Roles

| Factor | Consideration |
|--------|---------------|
| Job Functions | Can tasks be performed remotely? |
| Team Needs | Collaboration requirements |
| Customer Requirements | Face-to-face needs |
| Security | Data/system access requirements |
| Performance | Demonstrated productivity |

### Ineligible Roles

- Manufacturing/production
- Laboratory work requiring equipment
- Customer-facing roles requiring presence
- Classified work (ITAR/clearance)
- New employees (first 90 days)

